# Design Review Loop

Before creating or modifying any user interface, perform a structured design review.

Never generate UI immediately.

## Step 1 — Understand

User role, business objective, primary workflow, frequency of use.

## Step 2 — Inspect existing design

Layout, components, typography, spacing, navigation, colors, icons.

Prefer extending existing patterns.

## Step 3 — Information hierarchy

Primary → Secondary → Supporting → Rarely used.

## Step 4 — Component review

Does it exist? Can it be extended? Can it become reusable? Never duplicate UI.

## Step 5 — Layout review

Hierarchy, spacing, alignment, responsive behavior, whitespace, readability.

## Step 6 — Interaction review

Hover, focus, active, loading, success, error, disabled, empty.

## Step 7 — Accessibility

Keyboard, focus, semantic HTML, contrast, ARIA where required.

## Step 8 — Final questions

Is it simple? Is the workflow obvious? Is the hierarchy clear? Does it match the design system? Would a first-time user understand it?

Every new screen should strengthen the design system.
